welcome to the League of Legends  champion spotlight featuring Brock the  heart of the Freljord  if at first you do not succeed please  tell me what did his life rob is a hero  of the Freljord a champion strongman  famed for his selfless and legendary  feats once a simple goat herder Brom  found an unbreakable door and uses it as  a shield to protect man and creature  alike on his journey through runeterra  in game Brom is a tanky support with the  ability to defend allies from a barrage  of attacks before hammering out his own  immense crowd control abilities father  always big things come in small packages  whenever Brom attacks an enemy he  applies a stack of his passive  concussive blows if Brom dishes out four  blows to the head he deals in bursts of  magic damage and stuns his enemy for a  brief period after Brahms basic attacks  against them feel extra magic damage  although they won't receive additional  stacks of concussive blows there are two  things worth noting here first brahms  allies can help trigger the stun with  basic attacks and on hit abilities  second Bronk initiate concussive blows  against multiple enemies simultaneously  Brahms Q is winters bite Brom punches  his shield sending out a frozen skill  shot that damages and heavily slows the  first enemy struck winters bite also  applies concussive blows  giving him the opportunity to stun  distant enemies  winters bite is essential for gaining  Lane dominance tag your opponents with  it from range to give your marksman  opportunities for great trades Brahms W  is stand behind me targeted ability that  Brom can only use on himself and his  friends stand behind me since Brahma  leaping to an allied champion or minion  giving him and his ally bonus armor and  magic resistance  note that Brom will automatically stand  between his target and the nearest enemy  champion allowing him to fabulously  block skill shots with his awesome body  seriously check out those pecs you stand  behind me whenever you're separated from  your allies since it allows you to cross  over terrain you can keep yourself in a  good position while buffing their  defenses unbreakable Brahms II is his  signature defensive ability on  activation from raises his shield in a  target direction for a few seconds  blocking all damage from the first  incoming attack or spell any subsequent  damage from that direction is reduced by  a percentage while the shield remains  active the most notable thing about  unbreakable is that brahms shield  intercepts and stops all incoming  projectiles even those targeted allies  behind him  this allows broth to tank damage and  crowd control effects for his team  here's one nuance worth pointing out  though unbreakable doesn't intercept non  projectile abilities he does reduce the  damage he takes provided his shield is  facing the source of the damage  for example if unbreakable faces the  center of zyra's ultimate fraud will  take reduced damage but he won't prevent  damage to his allies braum can cast  other abilities and moves slightly  faster while the shield is raised and  keeps his shield pointed at the initial  target direction regardless of his  movement finally as awesome as  unbreakable is it's not awesome enough  to block turret attacks or true damage  unbreakable can negate major area of  effect spells for your teammates save if  our hard-hitting Ultimates to block off  a barrage of attacks brahms ultimate is  glacial fissure braum slams his shield  into the ground sending out a huge shock  wave that knocks up damages and slows  enemies in alive enemy units immediately  around Brahm are knocked up  significantly higher than enemies  further away if there are no enemy  champions immediately around Brahm the  first champion in the shock wave is  knocked up higher instead glacial  fissure also leaves behind a large zone  of ice that slows all enemies glacial  fissure is great for disengaging from  teamfights the ability creates a slow  zone that will handicap your opponent's  especially in the narrow corridors of  the jungle  braum strikes his own destiny one of his  many ability stand behind me is an  extremely versatile skill that has  several offensive and defensive options  when paired with the rest of his kit  let's look at a few important plays  you'll need in order to become master of  the mustache  the first is blocking for an ally  determine what direction the most damage  or crowd control is coming from then  leap in to get between danger and your  ally before using unbreakable to disrupt  the attack  this is your basic defensive pattern for  clutch saves and requires good timing  when assisting allies in a chase or  aggressive play you stand behind me  instead as a gap closer by choosing an  ally closest to your enemy you can often  put yourself in range to slow them with  winters bite since the - automatically  places you on the side closest to your  enemy you have an easier time lining up  the skill shot  you can also jump to allied minions  allowing for some tricky plays in Lane  finally if one of your friends gets  caught out in a bad situation surrounded  by enemy champions rom can come to the  rescue  you stand behind me to jump to the  center of the action then knock up and  slow everyone around your ally with your  oldsman this will give your team a  chance to disengage or allow other  allies to step in and help if needed  in Lane a successful Grom will  constantly look for opportunities to  stack his passive for a stun by tagging  Jonna with winters bite he makes it easy  for Quinn to follow up and pick her off  with the bonus damage and stun turning  his attention to Vayne he stacks  concussive blows with another Q and  basic attacks helping focus her down  before she can land the killing blow on  Quinn Brom is especially adept at  helping allies survive ganks with his W  and E as soon as Quinn is caught out he  immediately used to stand behind me to  boost her defenses and help her survive  focus fire from Pantheon and Vayne  note that Brom makes sure to stay behind  Quinn while using unbreakable so he can  tank any attacks directed at her forcing  Vayne to hit him instead as they retreat  brahms unbreakable completely negates  damage from the first attack or spell  that hits him so with careful timing you  can effectively cancel your opponent's  most damaging attack here Brom blocks  the gold card and the damage reduction  gives him just enough defense to survive  braum excels when sticking close to his  allies as soon as twitch appears Brom  repositions to the front of his Marchman  ready to not only intercept witches  damage but also hit both enemies with  glacial fissure rather than chase four  kills Brom sticks with Eze reel and  applies concussive blows to any of his  targets when playing Brom your goal  isn't so much to dive on the enemy as it  is to keep your squishy friends un'  squashed stand behind me slow cooldown  allows Brom multiple chances to  reposition and help allies in log  teamfights  in this example rom quickly finds  himself singled out after committing to  the fend Garen he uses stand behind me  to jump to misfortune and although he  dies he helps MF pick up the triple kill  a well-played braum boldly throws  himself in harm's way to protect his  friends when timed correctly unbreakable  has a potential to shield allies against  tons of damage with great positioning  here Brom turns a lethal AoE combo into  more of a mild annoyance almost  single-handedly turning the tide of this  fight  groms big heart needs a lot of  protection focus on health armor and  magic resistance tenacity is also  especially helpful since unbreakable  means Brom will be tanking crowd control  meant for his allies mixin cooldown  reduction to maximize Brom zone crowd  controlled and you'll have a heavy  frontline specialist ready to defend  against any amount of aggression or  unexpected bear wrestling thanks for  tuning into the Brom champion spotlight 